; Human-owned policy for B3: what a program may request, and what each sink may receive.
; The card's last four digits are personal data: the payment store may hold them, the audit log may not.
; Sinks are deny-by-default. Everything else a refund touches is public or internal.

(policy
  (allow store (ns "payments/*"))
  (allow audit)

  (sink store:payments (accepts pii))
  (sink audit          (accepts internal))

  ; Approved for QA (REFUND-411): whether the audit log has an event may depend on the card being the QA test card.
  (declassify qa-test-card
    (from pii) (to internal)
    (reason "QA test cards (ending 0000) are not audited; the absence of an event reveals only that the card is the test card.")
    (fns refund)
    (max-bits 1)))
